# Q2. What are the different deployment strategies?
"Deployment strategies are different ways of releasing a new version of application with minimum downtime and risk. The main deployment strategies are 
Blue-Green Deployment, 
Rolling Deployment, 
Canary Deployment, 
Recreate Deployment, 
and A/B Testing. The choice of strategy depends on the application's requirements and the level of risk we can accept."
> If the interviewer asks, "Can you explain each one?"
1. Recreate Deployment:
"The old version is stopped first, and then the new version is deployed, so there is some downtime."
2. Rolling Deployment:
"The new version is deployed one server at a time, which reduces downtime."
3. Blue-Green Deployment:
"Two identical environments are used, and traffic is switched to the new version after testing."
4. Canary Deployment:
"The new version is released to a small group of users first, and then to everyone if it works well."
5. A/B Testing:
"Two versions are shown to different users to compare performance and choose the better one."


# Q
3. What steps do you follow before migrating an application to the cloud?
Analyze the application – Understand the application and its dependencies.
Choose the cloud platform – Select AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.
Plan the infrastructure – Decide the required servers, storage, and database.
Take a backup – Back up the application and database.
Configure security – Set up IAM, firewall, and network settings.
Test before migration – Verify that everything is ready before moving to the cloud.


4. What challenges did you face during migration and how did you resolve them?
Database connection issue – I verified the connection string and database configuration.
Environment variable issue – I updated the environment variables correctly.
Deployment error – I checked the logs and fixed the configuration issues.
Application testing – I tested all the features after deployment to ensure everything worked properly. 

5. How do you minimize downtime during cloud migration?
 "To minimize downtime, I plan the migration carefully, take a backup, test the application before going live, and switch users to the new environment only after verifying that everything is working correctly."

6. How do you validate that the migrated application is working correctly?
 "After migration, I verify that the application is running correctly by testing all the features, checking the database connection, reviewing the logs, monitoring performance, and confirming that users can access the application without any issues."


# 2. Containerization (Docker, Kubernetes & Microservices)

Q1. Explain containerization and microservices architecture using Docker and Kubernetes.
"Containerization ka matlab hai application ko uski saari dependencies ke saath package karna, taaki wo har environment me same tarah se chale. Iske liye Docker use hota hai. Microservices architecture me ek bade application ko chhote-chhote independent services me divide kiya jata hai. In sab containers ko deploy, manage aur scale karne ke liye Kubernetes use hota hai."

Q2. What is the difference between a Virtual Machine and a Docker Container?
"Virtual Machine ke andar apna khud ka operating system hota hai, isliye wo heavy hoti hai aur start hone me time lagta hai. Docker Container host operating system ko share karta hai, isliye wo lightweight hota hai aur bahut jaldi start ho jata hai."

Q3. Why do we use Kubernetes instead of Docker alone?
"Docker sirf container banane aur run karne ke liye use hota hai. Agar bahut saare containers ho jayein, to unhe manage karna difficult ho jata hai. Kubernetes un containers ko automatically deploy, scale, load balance aur restart karta hai." 

Q4. Explain the lifecycle of a Docker container.
"Sabse pehle Docker image create karte hain. Us image se container run karte hain. Container application ko run karta hai. Jab zarurat na ho, to container ko stop, restart ya remove kar sakte hain."

Q5. How do Docker and Kubernetes work together?
"Docker application ko container ke andar package karta hai, aur Kubernetes un containers ko deploy, manage, scale aur monitor karta hai, taaki application smoothly run kare."

6. How would you deploy a microservices application using Kubernetes?
"Sabse pehle main har microservice ka Docker image banata hoon aur usse Docker Hub par push karta hoon. Uske baad Kubernetes ke Deployment aur Service files create karke cluster me deploy karta hoon. Finally, check karta hoon ki saare pods aur services sahi se run kar rahe hain aur application properly work kar rahi hai."


